    "#1.A What is NumPy, and why is it widely used in Python\n",
    "'''\n",
    "Def: \n",
    "NumPy (Numerical Python) is a core Python library used for \"numerical computing\" and \"handling large,\n",
    "multi-dimensional arrays and matrices\".\n",
    "\n",
    "- Its main feature is the n-dimensional array (ndarray), which stores homogeneous data (same type)\n",
    "in contiguous memory for high performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "-It also offers tools for linear algebra, statistics, random number generation, and Fourier transforms\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses of python:\n",
    "\n",
    "Speed – It performs mathematical operations much faster than regular Python lists.\n",
    "\n",
    "Vectorization – Allows operations on whole arrays without writing loops.\n",
    "\n",
    "Memory Efficiency – Uses less memory, making it suitable for large datasets.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rich Functions – Offers built-in math, statistics, and linear algebra tools.\n",
    "\n",
    "Ecosystem Support – Forms the base for libraries like Pandas, SciPy, and TensorFlow.\n",
    "\n",
    "'''"
   ]
