    "#2. A How does broadcasting work in NumPy\n",
    "'''\n",
    "Broadcasting allows NumPy to perform operations on arrays of different shapes \"without explicitly\n",
    "\n",
    "duplicating data\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Automatic Expansion – When two arrays have \"mismatched shapes\", NumPy automatically “stretches” the \n",
    "smaller array along the needed dimension for the operation.\n",
    "\n",
    "Shape Matching Rule – NumPy compares shapes from \"right to left\". Two dimensions are compatible if \n",
    "they are equal or one of them is 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "No Actual Copying – Even though it behaves like the smaller array expands, NumPy \"does not physically \n",
    "copy data\", making operations memory-efficient.\n",
    "\n",
    "Enables Vectorized Operations – Broadcasting supports fast, loop-free calculations across arrays of \n",
    "different sizes.\n",
    "\n",
    "'''"
   ]
