    "#8.What does the term “vectorized operation” mean in NumPy?\n",
    "'''\n",
    "A vectorized operation is a \"computation applied to entire arrays at once\", \"without writing explicit \n",
    "loops\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Loop-Free Processing – NumPy performs the looping internally in optimized C code, making operations fast.\n",
    "\n",
    "Element-wise Execution – The same operation is automatically applied to every element of the array.\n",
    "\n",
    "Improved Speed – Vectorization significantly reduces execution time compared to Python loops.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cleaner Code – Makes numerical expressions more readable and similar to standard mathematical notation.\n",
    "\n",
    "'''\n"
