    "#17.Explain the difference between apply() and map() in Pandas?\n",
    "'''\n",
    "Scope of Use\n",
    "\n",
    "map() – Primarily used on Series to apply a function element-wise.\n",
    "\n",
    "apply() – Can be used on both Series and DataFrames; applies a function along an axis (rows or columns).\n",
    "\n",
    "Function Flexibility\n",
    "\n",
    "map() – Accepts functions, dictionaries, or Series for element-wise transformation.\n",
    "\n",
    "apply() – Can handle more complex functions, including aggregations across rows or columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "Return Type\n",
    "\n",
    "map() – Always returns a Series.\n",
    "\n",
    "apply() – Returns a Series for Series input or a DataFrame for DataFrame input.\n",
    "\n",
    "Typical Use Case\n",
    "\n",
    "map() – Converting values, replacing elements, or simple element-wise operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "apply() – Row/column-level computations, aggregations, or custom transformations.\n",
    "\n",
    "'''"
   ]
